WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Attendee · Create an incident
The attendee describes a fictional ankle injury and keeps “Use my location”. The recording sandbox supplies fictional GPS.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Attendee · Report received
I-1 is saved. “Send report only” does not automatically request a volunteer; Mo can offer the incident manually.

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Mo · New incident on the map
The same incident appears as an orange pin beside Priya’s blue volunteer pin. Mo opens I-1 from the map.

4
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.000
Mo · Offer to Priya
Mo reviews the original report, chooses available Priya and sends an offer.

5
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Volunteer · Incoming offer
Priya receives the incident details and destination. She has Accept and Decline controls.

6
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Volunteer · Accept the assignment
Priya accepts. The server assigns I-1 to her and marks her busy. Arrival still needs confirmation.

7
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Volunteer · Grey dotted connection
The volunteer’s field map draws a decorative dotted curve between the starting ping and attendee.

8
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.000
Mo · Start fictional movement
Mo starts the existing 90-second movement demo. This is simulated movement, not real phone GPS.

9
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Volunteer · Journey begins
Priya’s simulated moving pin advances. The grey dotted path starts gaining white fill.

10
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Volunteer · White progress advances
White centres extend along the same dotted curve as the simulated volunteer approaches.

11
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Volunteer · Approaching the destination
The replay skips time between captured frames of the real app’s 90-second simulation.

12
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Volunteer · Full white progress
The backend reaches 100% and the dotted connection is filled white. The incident remains open.

13
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Mo · Same journey visible
Mo sees the incident, volunteer and completed decorative progress in the operations map.

14
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Attendee · Private responder tracking
The attendee sees the frozen volunteer starting ping and white progress, without the volunteer’s moving pin.

15
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Volunteer · Human confirmation remains
At 100%, Priya still has “Mark arrived”. Movement never automatically confirms arrival or resolves the incident.
